Z||000005||Raydar||11-17-2001||04:12 PM||||Very cool!<P>If you want restoration parts, try these folks...  <A HREF="http://www.yearone.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.yearone.com</A> <P>Their online site is kind of poor, but their catalogs are huge! Lots of good stuff. <P>They are located in the Southeastern US. (Across town from me, actually.)<P>They have reproduction hood tachs. Very good quality, but not inexpensive.<P>If you <I>really</I> don't want to buy a catalog, I can look up the part number of the hood tach for you.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||GTFiero1||11-17-2001||08:21 PM||||ystbrother who is coming out of the military in Dec. has a 68 GTO, he is in california now but coming back here and i'll get to ride in it! yahoo!<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SwissFormula||11-18-2001||05:01 PM||||Nice to get some positive feedback<BR>and help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Since i do not live in the USA, buying a catalog wont help me much. I know  shops that import parts for american cars. They have all necessary catalogs & they can import everything i'm willing to pay for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>I've seen reproduction hood tachs, as you say "not inexpensive". A 200$ part costs me 300$, thats for taxes & shipping...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>oh yeah, more pictures coming soon!<BR>Thanx & good night...<BR>Roy<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula, T-Top<BR>1 of 20 Fieros in Switzerland||||reg||1
